=== SURVEY ===
Web source components/ui/Slider.tsx is a single-thumb slider primitive wrapping a controlled
`<input type="range">`. Props: value, min, max, step (=1), onChange, label (required — the visible
`<label>` AND the accessible name), formatValue? (formats the readout + `aria-valuetext`), showLabel
(=true), disabled?, id? (auto from `useId`), className?. Render: a `space-y-1` wrapper → (when
showLabel) a `flex justify-between` row [`<label>` text-secondary on the leading edge, the formatted
value `text-muted tabular-nums` on the trailing edge] → an `h-9` track row holding the range input
(`accent-cyan-500`, focus ring, `disabled:opacity-50`). Behaviour: the change handler does
`const next = Number(value); if (!Number.isNaN(next)) onChange(next)`; `display = formatValue ?
formatValue(value) : String(value)`; `aria-valuetext={display}`; `aria-label={label}` only when
showLabel is false. The JSDoc documents the WAI-ARIA APG keyboard pattern the browser services:
Arrow keys step by `step`, PageUp/Down by ~10% of the range, Home/End jump to min/max.
Data sources (P1/S8): useId — ID generation, NOT a data fetch. Shared components: none. Charts/maps:
none. i18n keys extracted from source: none (the surface is anonymous — label + value are
caller-supplied).
Existing native: no Slider/SliderField/SliderModel/SliderInput/SliderProjection/SliderMath/
SliderMeta/SliderTelemetry/SliderStrings/SliderAccessibility symbols anywhere in the app (grep clean →
no collision). An atomic `TSSlider` exists in Sources/Components/UI/Sliders.swift, but that is the P4
component-library bundle's concern (explicitly Out of Scope here); this surface is the instrumented
shared-surface tier (state-holder + telemetry + i18n + projection + tests), the same split as
CurrencyInputField (0150) vs. the atomic field.
Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/Range (0087) — the closest precedent, a synchronous
no-fetch primitive (Adapter/Model/Projection/Views/Previews/strings/Tests/AdapterTests) — and
CurrencyInput (0150) for the controlled value + onChange commit seam.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is a controlled primitive with NO data dependency: it reads its `value` prop and
  `useId`, and emits `onChange`. `useId` is id generation, not a query. There is therefore NO
  loading / error / stale / offline axis in the source. Per the committed precedent for synchronous
  no-fetch surfaces (Range 0087, Distance 0085, AnimatedNumber 0075), synthesising network chrome
  here would INVENT state the source does not have — a parity violation, not parity. The genuine
  render branches reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surface, the track always shows):
    • showLabel = true  → label + live readout row over the track.
    • showLabel = false → track only; `label` preserved as the accessible name (web `aria-label`).
    • disabled          → dimmed (opacity 0.5, web `disabled:opacity-50`) + non-interactive.
  The value is a required prop, so there is no empty/missing-value branch. This disposition is stated
  in Slider.Adapter's header so it is not silent.
- Native idiom: the SwiftUI parity of `<input type="range">` is `SwiftUI.Slider`. The public view is
  named `SliderField` (not `Slider`) to avoid shadowing `SwiftUI.Slider` — the same disambiguation
  the sibling `RangeReadout` (0087) and `CurrencyInputField` (0150) apply; the file keeps the surface
  name (Slider.*) and the diagnostics slug stays "Slider".
- Architecture mirrors the Range leaf:
    • Adapter (pure, Foundation): SliderResolve i18n seam; SliderMeta (slug + step default + ~10%
      page fraction + the `useId` id resolution); SliderInput value-type snapshot; SliderCommand
      (the APG key set); SliderMath (effective step/maximum, clamp, snap-to-step, the sanitize order
      snap→clamp, the PageUp/Down large step, and per-command transitions — the browser's range-input
      numeric semantics); SliderFormatting (the `String(value)` default + the `Number(value)` parse);
      SliderAccessibility (name/value passthrough + the localized hint).
    • Projection: SliderResolved + SliderProjection.resolve(input, format, strings) — canonical value,
      formatted readout, label/value/hint a11y, and a degenerate-range-safe control range.
    • Model: SliderTelemetry seam (+ OSLog default) for the once-only view.opened; SliderStrings i18n
      facade; @Observable @MainActor SliderModel (value, setValue→onChange, apply(command), sync,
      start/stop). No async source — the host owns the value (web controlled component).
    • View (SliderField) + Views (SliderLabelRow, SliderTrackView) + Previews + strings +
      Tests + AdapterTests.
- Keyboard parity: SwiftUI.Slider(step:) services Arrow stepping + the VoiceOver increment/decrement
  natively; the PageUp/PageDown + Home/End jumps are wired as `.onKeyPress` commands and an
  `.accessibilityAdjustableAction`, all routed through the pure SliderMath transitions (unit tested).
- i18n: the source renders no translatable copy of its own (label + value are caller-owned). The one
  native-owned string is a VoiceOver adjust hint (a refinement over the web `<input>`, which has
  none), resolved through the injected P1/S10 facade — so no English is hardcoded in Swift.
- Rejected: porting Tailwind classes literally (used P1/S9 tokens); reusing the atomic TSSlider (Out
  of Scope, and it would shrink the testable parity surface); synthesising loading/error/stale/offline
  chrome (would invent non-existent source state — see Range/Distance/AnimatedNumber precedent);
  reading/writing the value directly in the view (routed through the model + onChange).

